      "writtenOn": "2025-06-02T20:45:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**If this comment is right, the other ones don\u0027t matter.**\n\nIn ciri\u0027s current sourcing policy, as implemented in `dpm_get_source_pdo` above, a port will always offer 3A if it can. There is no scenario where it could offer more current, but it hasn\u0027t yet. Therefore, I think the present PDP should always be equal to the reported PDP, and you don\u0027t need to check anything extra here.\n\nAnother way of putting this: `dpm_get_source_pdo` is already checking exactly what you want to check here, and the added `max_current_claimed_bitmask` logic is just trying to match that existing logic. But we can just rely upon the result of `dpm_get_source_pdo` to reuse the existing logic. Then we wouldn\u0027t need any of the additional logic currently in this CL.\n\nDoes it work to just set `port_present_pdp \u003d port_reported_pdp`?",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "f4e41cb1_64072de8",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "zephyr/program/geralt/ciri/src/usbc.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 121,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 125,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tif (can_supply_max_current(port)) {\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "085656b3935b3fb1314cc28ba3c35bf533e86098",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
